Subject: PackageAbiHelperImpl: install an arm64-v8a only multiArch app while ARM translation is on

derivePackageAbi chooses the ABI of a multiArch app that targets Android 15 or later from the
natively supported 64-bit ABIs only: Build.SUPPORTED_64_BIT_ABIS without each ABI a native
bridge translates. With ARM translation on, the DSA guest's 64-bit ABIs are x86_64 and arm64-v8a
(arm64-v8a through the bridge), so that list was x86_64 alone, and Google Play's arm64-v8a only
multiArch apps were refused with INSTALL_FAILED_MULTI_ARCH_NOT_MATCH_ALL_NATIVE_ABIS although the
translator runs them.

getNativelySupported64BitAbis now returns Build.SUPPORTED_64_BIT_ABIS, in its order: x86_64
first, then arm64-v8a while translation is on. An app with x86_64 code is installed as x86_64 as
before. With translation off the list is x86_64 alone, so nothing changes. make-image.py made
this change as a dex edit of the published services.jar until the image took the framework
build's.

Applies to frameworks/base at 45034f0663f960d9ee5fb0a101a4732b71f6e2f4 (Android 16).
---
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java
@@ -335,13 +335,14 @@ final class PackageAbiHelperImpl implements PackageAbiHelper {
         return sNativelySupported32BitAbis;
     }

+    // DSA: every 64-bit ABI the guest lists, the ones a native bridge translates included, in
+    // Build.SUPPORTED_64_BIT_ABIS's order. derivePackageAbi chooses a multiArch app's ABI from
+    // this list, and refused an app with arm64-v8a code only while ARM translation was on,
+    // although the translator runs it as it runs every other arm64-v8a app. x86_64 comes first,
+    // so an app with x86_64 code is still installed as x86_64; with translation off the list is
+    // x86_64 alone, as before.
     private static String[] getNativelySupported64BitAbis() {
-        if (sNativelySupported64BitAbis != null) {
-            return sNativelySupported64BitAbis;
-        }
-
-        sNativelySupported64BitAbis = getNativelySupportedAbis(Build.SUPPORTED_64_BIT_ABIS);
-        return sNativelySupported64BitAbis;
+        return Build.SUPPORTED_64_BIT_ABIS;
     }

     @Override
